  "slug": "learning-quantum-40ee",
  "summary": "New preprints tackle exponential concentration, measurement-free Riemannian training, backprop-free quantum Transformers and transferable circuit search.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is making quantum learning models trainable and scalable without relying on standard variational gradient loops. One scheme performs Riemannian gradient optimization autonomously, without measurements or classical feedback. A fully quantum Transformer uses SVD-based non-unitary circuits and quantum nonlinear activations and is trained by multi-agent RL without backpropagation. On trainability, an empirical study of fidelity and projected quantum kernels and quantum extreme learning examines how entanglement, locality and bandwidth scaling govern exponential concentration. On expressivity, contractive layers add all-to-all couplings with one trainable parameter on Rydberg arrays. Architecture design is increasingly learned: LatentRL-QAS transfers circuit designs across qubit counts via latent-space RL, and an ML workflow extrapolates gate, measurement and reset syntax to scale holographic circuits. Adjacent work covers dephasing-based minimal quantum reservoirs, JEPA world models inferring Hamiltonian parameters, single-ancilla estimation of multi-time correlators, and a QCBM prior guiding classical network training. All are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
